From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: drop the invented camera rail parents

The PM8009 camera rails added here were given vdd-l1, vdd-l3 and vdd-l4 parents
pointing at vreg_s8c_1p3, chosen because that is what ldo2 uses. No board in the
tree describes those parents: every one that carries PM8009 declares only
vdd-l2-supply, and the other mainline SM8150 handset with this PMIC describes
only ldo2, ldo5 and ldo6.

The three camera slots fed by these rails reset the handset when powered, while
the slot fed by ldo2 comes up cleanly. Since the parents were an inference with
nothing behind it, describe the rails the way every other board does and leave
them out.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
@@ -394,10 +394,7 @@
 		vdd-s1-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
 		vdd-s2-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
 
-		vdd-l1-supply = <&vreg_s8c_1p3>;
 		vdd-l2-supply = <&vreg_s8c_1p3>;
-		vdd-l3-supply = <&vreg_s8c_1p3>;
-		vdd-l4-supply = <&vreg_s8c_1p3>;
 		vdd-l5-l6-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
 
 		vreg_l1f_1p1: ldo1 {
--
2.50.1
